<div id="S4.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ablation analysis of the AMAS architecture</span>  To rigorously assess the architectural integrity of our AMAS framework, we systematically evaluate three distinct modifications: (a) AMAS-1, which employs <math id="S4.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=8</annotation></semantics></math> top-ranked graph candidates; (b) AMAS-2, which restricts candidate selection to <math id="S4.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=2</annotation></semantics></math> top graphs; (c) AMAS-3, which omits the weight coefficient <math id="S4.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> from the loss formulation (Equation <a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.3 Construction of graph designer ‣ 3 AMAS ‣ AMAS: Adaptively Determining Communication Topology for LLM-based Multi-Agent System" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>). Comparative results across Crossword and Game-of-24 benchmarks are documented in Table <a href="#S4.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ 4.5 Ablation studies and further analysis ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ AMAS: Adaptively Determining Communication Topology for LLM-based Multi-Agent System" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. Notably, the baseline AMAS configuration (mirroring Table <a href="#S4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 4.3 Experiment Settings ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ AMAS: Adaptively Determining Communication Topology for LLM-based Multi-Agent System" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) achieves superior performance over all alternative implementations. Specifically: (a) AMAS-1 and AMAS-2 analyses confirm <math id="S4.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=4</annotation></semantics></math> as the optimal candidate threshold—reducing (<math id="S4.SS5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=2</annotation></semantics></math>) or expanding (<math id="S4.SS5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=8</annotation></semantics></math>) this parameter degrades graph designer efficacy. (b) The AMAS-3 comparison substantiates the loss objective’s design (Equation <a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.3 Construction of graph designer ‣ 3 AMAS ‣ AMAS: Adaptively Determining Communication Topology for LLM-based Multi-Agent System" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), where <math id="S4.SS5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> quantifies item-wise disparity (<math id="S4.SS5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="S4.SS5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>), thereby sharpening the model’s sensitivity to ordinal relationships within the ranking structure.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T5" class="ltx_table">
<div id="S4.T5.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:117.3pt;height:38.1pt;vertical-align:-17.5pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-36.1pt,11.7pt) scale(0.619052354939488,0.619052354939488) ;">
<table id="S4.T5.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
